<title>AUSTRALIA: CRICKET-AUSTRALIA 139 FOR TWO AT STUMPS V WEST INDIES.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-AUSTRALIA 139 FOR TWO AT STUMPS V WEST INDIES.</headline>
<dateline>ADELAIDE 1997-01-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia were 139 for two at the close of play on the first day of their fourth test match against West Indies at the Adelaide Oval on Saturday, having earlier dismissed the West Indies for 130.</p>
<p>Scores:</p>
<p>Australia - 139 for two from 40 overs (Matthew Hayden 66 not out)</p>
<p>West Indies - 130 in 47.5 overs (Michael Bevan four for 31, Shane Warne three for 42.)</p>
